## Benchmark v2 — sub-second per-shard timing (the v1 CPU column above is quantization-inflated)
## v1 used `date +%s`: 360 shards x 1 s granularity, and raising D2 makes each shard walk D2x more
## roots so fewer finish under a second and more round UP — biased against D2>1 specifically. The
## tell is k=7 v1: cpu 1598 s at D2=4 but 1190 s at D2=8; a duplication cost cannot FALL as D2 rises.
